## SCOPE CONTRACT 4: ERROR HANDLING & MONITORING (HIGH)
**Priority:** P1  
**Owner:** [TBD]  
**Estimated Duration:** 3 days  
**Dependencies:** Scope 3 (type safety)

### Current State
- `app/error.tsx` - Generic error page, no error logging
- `app/500.tsx` - Minimal error page, no details
- Sentry React SDK installed (`@sentry/react` in package.json) but NO integration
- No error correlation IDs
- No structured logging

### Target State
- Sentry integrated with error tracking
- Error boundaries capture and report errors
- All API routes have structured error logging
- Error correlation IDs for support debugging
- Health check endpoint for monitoring

### Scope Contract
**IN SCOPE:**
- Integrate Sentry in `app/error.tsx` and `app/500.tsx`
- Add Sentry error reporting to API routes
- Implement error correlation ID generation
- Add structured logging wrapper (replace console.*)
- Create `/api/health` endpoint for monitoring
- Add error boundary to checkout flow (critical)
- Add error boundary to product pages

**OUT OF SCOPE:**
- Performance monitoring (separate scope)
- Custom error analytics dashboard
- Alerting configuration (Sentry handles this)

### Definition of Done
**LAYER 1 - CODE COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Sentry initialized in error boundaries
- [ ] `app/error.tsx` reports to Sentry with context
- [ ] API routes use structured logging (not console.log)
- [ ] Error correlation ID attached to all requests
- [ ] `/api/health` endpoint returns 200 with status
- [ ] Checkout flow has error boundary with recovery

**LAYER 2 - TESTING COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Unit test: Error boundary catches and reports
- [ ] Unit test: Structured logging outputs correct format
- [ ] Integration test: Health endpoint returns correct response
- [ ] Mock Sentry client for testing

**LAYER 3 - VERIFICATION COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Manual test: Trigger error, verify Sentry receives it
- [ ] Manual test: Error correlation ID appears in logs
- [ ] Manual test: Health endpoint returns 200
- [ ] Sentry dashboard shows errors from local dev

**LAYER 4 - DOCUMENTATION COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Error handling patterns documented
- [ ] Sentry setup documented
- [ ] Health endpoint usage documented

### Verification Methods
```bash
# Automated verification
npm run test:error-handling
npm run test:health-endpoint

# Manual verification checklist
# [ ] Error in dev triggers Sentry report
# [ ] Error correlation ID in response headers
# [ ] Health endpoint: curl /api/health returns {"status":"ok"}
# [ ] Checkout error shows user-friendly message
```

