## SCOPE CONTRACT 7: SECURITY & MIDDLEWARE HARDENING (MEDIUM)
**Priority:** P2  
**Owner:** [TBD]  
**Estimated Duration:** 3 days  
**Dependencies:** None

### Current State
- `middleware.ts` - Basic Clerk middleware, minimal security
- No rate limiting on API routes
- No CSRF protection for mutations
- No request size limits
- Security headers present but basic

### Target State
- Rate limiting on checkout and API routes
- CSRF protection for mutations
- Request size limits enforced
- Security headers complete (CSP, HSTS)
- Input validation on all API routes

### Scope Contract
**IN SCOPE:**
- Add rate limiting middleware (checkout API, webhooks)
- Add request size limits (10MB max)
- Add CSRF protection for mutation endpoints
- Enhance security headers (CSP, HSTS, Permissions-Policy)
- Add input validation using Zod on all API routes
- Add IP-based abuse detection (basic)
- Sanitize all user inputs

**OUT OF SCOPE:**
- Advanced WAF rules
- DDoS protection (handled by hosting provider)
- Penetration testing (separate engagement)

### Definition of Done
**LAYER 1 - CODE COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Rate limiting implemented on `/api/checkout`
- [ ] Rate limiting implemented on `/api/webhook`
- [ ] Request size limit middleware added
- [ ] CSRF protection added to mutations
- [ ] Zod validation on all API route inputs
- [ ] Security headers enhanced in `next.config.ts`

**LAYER 2 - TESTING COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Unit test: Rate limiting blocks excessive requests
- [ ] Unit test: CSRF protection rejects invalid tokens
- [ ] Unit test: Input validation rejects malformed data
- [ ] Unit test: Request size limit enforced

**LAYER 3 - VERIFICATION COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Manual test: Rate limit triggers after threshold
- [ ] Manual test: Security headers present in responses
- [ ] Manual test: Invalid input rejected with 400
- [ ] Manual test: Large request rejected with 413

**LAYER 4 - DOCUMENTATION COMPLETE:**
- [ ] Security measures documented
- [ ] Rate limit thresholds documented
- [ ] Security headers explained

### Verification Methods
```bash
# Automated verification
npm run test:security

# Manual verification checklist
# [ ] curl -X POST /api/checkout (rapid requests) gets 429
# [ ] curl -X POST /api/checkout with large body gets 413
# [ ] Security headers present: curl -I / | grep -i "content-security\|strict-transport"
# [ ] Invalid JSON rejected: curl -X POST /api/checkout -d "invalid"
```

